    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d89">

                <pb facs="0233" n="121" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg121"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 18643/15.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Dudley to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 474.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith the
                        list<anchor n="1" xml:id="d89-f1"/> communicated to this Government, of
                    articles of American production proposed for preferential treatment. Of those
                    articles the following,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d89-f2"/> when imported into Brazil
                    during 1910, have been granted a reduction of 20 per cent from the general
                    tariff rates by an executive decree of the 15th instant, a translation of which
                    may be found herewith.</p>
                <p>The effect of the decree is to add to our preferential list, as it has stood
                    during the past few years, cement, dried fruits, alarm clocks, desks, corsets,
                    and furniture for schools.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Irving B. Dudley.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d89-a1.xml" xpointer="d89-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
